curriculum in intro

- basic unit circle identities

- tangent

- basic geo problems

- basic identities & practice (alg focus)

- inverse trig functions

- see the graphs of sine and cos? or save for later (learn to graph later)
    - REM the point is to start less challenging and get harder and harder later on!

level up

- remaining trig functions

- nuances of inverse trig functions

- harder trig in geo -- LoS, etc.

- geo practice, with some identities

- harder identities -- useful in alg and geo!
    - eg chebyshev, sum to product, etc.

- Brief touch on complex numbers (that should be separate)

**features**

- see also: eg radians, speck links
    - Don't understand something? Don't worry! We've all been there; don't be discouraged. One of these resources can likely help: <speck, external links, etc.>.

- summary! synopsis?, key ideas, key theorems

- **do the problems** lol


